---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { siteConfig } from "../config/site";
const lastUpdated = "2026-10-21";
---

<Layout title="Terms" description="Terms of use for TimeAtlas, including the limits of what its clocks, search, and globe can promise.">
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-4 py-10 sm:px-6">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-paper-100">Terms of use</h1>

    <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-paper-600">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

    <section class="mt-8">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-paper-100">What TimeAtlas is for</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-paper-300">
        TimeAtlas is an informational tool for comparing times across time zones. It is
        provided for general convenience and is not a substitute for an authoritative source
        when precision genuinely matters — for example, legal deadlines, travel bookings, or
        anything where being off by the wrong offset or daylight-saving status would cause
        real harm.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-8">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-paper-100">No accuracy guarantee</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-paper-300">
        TimeAtlas's "Live" clocks depend on your own device's system clock and are not
        independently verified against any time authority. Time zone and daylight-saving data
        comes from your browser's built-in time zone database and can lag behind very recent
        real-world rule changes. Day/night shading on the globe is an approximation, not an
        astronomical calculation of actual sunrise or sunset. See the{" "}
        <a href="/guide/" class="underline hover:text-paper-100">guide</a> for the full detail.
        TimeAtlas is provided "as is," without warranty of accuracy, and{" "}
        {siteConfig.operatorName || "its operator"} disclaims liability for decisions made in
        reliance on it to the fullest extent permitted by law.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-8">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-paper-100">Acceptable use</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-paper-300">
        Don't use TimeAtlas to attempt to disrupt the service (for example, automated
        scraping at a volume that degrades it for other users), to circumvent any access
        controls, or for any unlawful purpose.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-8">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-paper-100">Third-party data and content</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-paper-300">
        TimeAtlas incorporates third-party geographic data under the licenses described on the{" "}
        <a href="/about/#data-sources" class="underline hover:text-paper-100">About page</a>.
        Those licenses, and the terms of the services TimeAtlas's fonts are loaded from,
        apply alongside these terms.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-8">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-paper-100">Changes</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-paper-300">
        These terms may be updated from time to time; the date above reflects the last
        change.
      </p>
    </section>

    {siteConfig.contactEmail && (
      <section class="mt-8">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-paper-100">Questions</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-paper-300">
          Email <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.contactEmail}`} class="underline hover:text-paper-100">{siteConfig.contactEmail}</a> with questions about this page.
        </p>
      </section>
    )}
  </article>
</Layout>
